One trace marker per frame at the input poll and the video callback

With RALAT set, RetroArch writes "ralat poll" when it polls the pad and
"ralat video" when the core hands it the frame, to the kernel's trace
marker. A trace of vblanks, flips and Mesa's commit markers then gives
read to first line per frame (documentation/LATENCY.md). Unset, it is
one getenv and a branch per call. runemu sets it from portareos.ralat.

--- a/input/input_driver.c
+++ b/input/input_driver.c
@@ -7675,11 +7675,29 @@
       for (i = 0; i < 9; i++)
          memcpy(&dst[i / 3][i % 3], &v[i], sizeof(float));
       return;
+   }
+}
+
+/* ralat: one trace marker per frame at the input poll and at the video
+ * callback, when RALAT is set, so a kernel trace of flips and vblanks
+ * can be paired with the poll each frame was emulated from. Test only. */
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+void ralat_mark(const char *s)
+{
+   static int fd = -2;
+   if (fd == -2)
+      fd = getenv("RALAT") ? open("/sys/kernel/tracing/trace_marker", O_WRONLY) : -1;
+   if (fd >= 0)
+   {
+      ssize_t n = write(fd, s, strlen(s));
+      (void)n;
    }
 }
 
